cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite it as below."
title: "fewshot-action-models: safe action-model learning from a few demonstrations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pigazzini
    given-names: Pasquale
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6977-7317"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.0.1
abstract: >-
  Learns the preconditions and effects of planning actions, a lifted STRIPS model with
  negative preconditions, from a few fully observed demonstrations by safe action-model
  learning (SAM); plans with the learned model by breadth-first search, cross-checked by an
  answer-set planner; and scores every plan against an independent reference model. A plan
  valid under the learned model is valid under the true one. The learning curve measures
  what that guarantee costs in solved problems on Blocksworld, Gripper and Logistics, and
  every published count is reproduced by a committed command.
repository-code: "https://github.com/ppigazzini/fewshot-action-models"
keywords:
  - action model learning
  - automated planning
  - STRIPS
  - PDDL
  - answer set programming
  - abstraction
